📊 Superstore Sales Analysis (Microsoft Excel)
Project Overview

This project analyzes the Superstore Sales dataset using Microsoft Excel to uncover trends in sales performance, customer segments, regions, product categories, and monthly sales.

The objective was to practice Excel data analysis techniques while generating business insights that can support data-driven decision-making.

Dataset
Source: Kaggle – Superstore Sales Dataset
Records: Sales transactions from a retail superstore
Tool Used: Microsoft Excel
Data Cleaning

Before analysis, the dataset was cleaned by:

Checking for duplicate records (none found)
Standardizing inconsistent date formats
Creating calculated columns for analysis
Converting the dataset into an Excel Table
Formatting numerical fields for consistency
Excel Skills Applied
Pivot Tables
Aggregate Functions (SUM, AVERAGE, COUNT, MAX, MIN)
IF Function
Data Cleaning
Sorting & Filtering
Table Formatting
Dashboard Design
Charts and Visualizations
Business Questions Answered
Which region generates the highest sales?
Which customer segment contributes the most revenue?
Which month records the highest sales?
Which product sub-category generates the most sales?
What are the total sales, average sales, highest sale, lowest sale, and total number of orders?
Key Insights
The Consumer segment generated the highest total sales.
The West region recorded the highest sales performance.
Sales peaked in November and December, indicating strong year-end demand.
Phones and Chairs were among the highest-selling product sub-categories.
Sales varied significantly across regions and customer segments, highlighting opportunities for targeted business strategies.
Dashboard Features

The dashboard includes:

Sales by Region
Sales by Customer Segment
Monthly Sales Trend
Sales by Product Sub-Category
KPI Cards
Total Sales
Average Sales
Maximum Sale
Minimum Sale
Total Orders
